On the other hand, in the contexts to which it is appropriate, it is needless ^^PURISM^^ to restrict its sense to what the words could mean in Latin, i. e. (a) & *the rest* as opposed to & *other things*, (b) *and* the like as opposed to *or* the like, (c) & other *things* as opposed to *persons*;
>>>

